======================================================================================================================
G2 -- is f_DM prior-driven?  (RC41 overlap, actual SED + gas)
======================================================================================================================
  Delta_prior = log M_bar,fit - log(M* + M_gas): median -0.097 dex (n = 41); Spearman rho(delta_flat, Delta_prior) = +0.33 (p = 0.036)
  Theil-Sen slope of delta_flat on Delta_prior +0.156; z-slope of delta_flat after removing it: +0.014 [-0.027, +0.069] (n = 41)
  -> prior-driven (|rho| >= 0.3 and p < 0.05): YES

======================================================================================================================
G3 -- the pressure term (V_c'^2 = V_c^2 - (3.36 - alpha) sigma0^2; g_bar fixed)
======================================================================================================================
  alpha = 3.36 (n = 100)             flat: slope -0.025 [-0.068, +0.010] (z: flat-true -1.3, rival-true -5.0); rival: slope -0.086 [-0.125, -0.050] (z: flat-true -1.4, rival-true -4.5)
  alpha = 1.68 (n = 100)             flat: slope -0.063 [-0.110, -0.023] (z: flat-true -2.9, rival-true -6.4); rival: slope -0.118 [-0.160, -0.076] (z: flat-true -2.6, rival-true -5.6)
  alpha = 0.0: 2 galaxies have V_c'^2 <= 0 (the fit's pressure term exceeds V_c^2) and are excluded from this variant
  alpha = 0.0 (n = 98)               flat: slope -0.093 [-0.135, -0.044] (z: flat-true -3.9, rival-true -7.3); rival: slope -0.141 [-0.189, -0.097] (z: flat-true -3.2, rival-true -5.9)
  the rival's deficit survives: alpha 3.36: YES; alpha 1.68: YES; alpha 0.0: YES

