======================================================================================================================
G5 -- can a z-dependent gas mis-scaling ALONE produce the pattern?  g_bar,analysis = g_bar,true x 10^(beta log10((1 + z)/2.5))
======================================================================================================================
  [PASS] C4 machinery: the flat-truth mock at beta = 0 gives slopes (0, expected) equal to the baseline expectations to 1e-9
         +0.00e+00, -0.058452 vs -0.058452
  M1 (flat truth): the mis-scaling that reproduces the observed delta_flat slope -0.025: beta = +0.184 -> differential dlog M_bar (z 0.6 -> 2.5) = +0.062 dex; the rival's slope there -0.081 (observed -0.086)
  M2 (rival truth): best beta = +0.719 (dlog M_bar = +0.244 dex) with chi2 = 0.02 (slopes -0.027, -0.085 vs observed -0.025, -0.086); within the plausible range |dlog M_bar| <= 0.2 dex (|beta| <= 0.59): best chi2 = 1.68 at beta = +0.58; at beta = 0: chi2 = 44.7
  -> M2 produces the pattern at a plausible mis-scaling (chi2 < 2 with |dlog M_bar| <= 0.2 dex): YES; the stress variant V1 (gas fraction fixed with z) corresponds to about -0.18 dex of differential M_bar

======================================================================================================================
G7 -- regress delta on log g_bar first (Theil-Sen), then the z-slope of the residuals
======================================================================================================================
  flat : slope on log g_bar -0.049 [-0.111, +0.024]; residual z-slope -0.023 [-0.058, +0.012] (expected if flat true +0.000, if rival true +0.072; z: -1.3 / -5.3)
  rival: slope on log g_bar +0.008 [-0.067, +0.093]; residual z-slope -0.087 [-0.123, -0.050] (expected if flat true -0.067, if rival true +0.000; z: -1.1 / -4.7)
  -> the rival's residual z-slope stays negative (CI upper < 0): YES

